\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 1. Why controlled enums are more reliable for filtering\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Example product metadata:\
\
heat_level = 4\
contains_allergens = ["peanuts"]\
If a user says:\
\'93No peanuts.\'94\
With metadata:\
\
WHERE NOT ('peanuts' = ANY(contains_allergens))\
This is deterministic.\uc0\u8232 Zero ambiguity.\u8232 Zero ranking uncertainty.\
Finding: Structured filters give binary guarantees (allowed / not allowed).\
Vectors cannot guarantee exclusion.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 2. Why vectors are not safe for hard constraints\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 If you rely only on embeddings:\
You embed:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93peanut-free snack\'94\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 product descriptions\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Similarity may still retrieve:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93Contains peanuts but loved by many\'94\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Because embeddings optimize 
\f0\b semantic proximity
\f1\b0 , not logical exclusion.\
Vectors are probabilistic.\uc0\u8232 Metadata filters are deterministic.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 3. Where vectors outperform structured filtering\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Now flip the example:\
User says:\
\'93Something cozy, savory, not too intense, good for watching movies.\'94\
There is no clean enum for:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 cozy\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 movie vibe\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 comforting\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Structured SQL cannot understand this.\
Embeddings can.\
Finding: Vectors are superior for fuzzy meaning.\uc0\u8232 Metadata is superior for rules.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 4. In ecommerce systems\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 There are two types of requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 A) Hard constraints (must never break)\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Allergies\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Price limit\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Stock availability\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Heat tolerance cap\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Volume capacity of a snack box\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These require structured metadata.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 B) Soft preferences (ranking signals)\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93I usually like umami\'94\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93I prefer crunchy\'94\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93I want something fun\'94\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 \'93Surprise me\'94\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 These are ideal for vector similarity + ranking.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 5. So is structured filtering \'93more effective\'94 than vectors?\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Not globally.\
More effective for:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Exclusions\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Numeric limits\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Legal constraints\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Inventory logic\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Less effective for:\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Taste similarity\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Emotional descriptors\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f2\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f1\fs26 Conversational nuance\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 They are complementary systems.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
